course: dictionary
lesson: 15393
title: Spherical: shaped like a ball
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spherical is a precise word for something shaped like a ball. When you meet it, read the words around it for clues. «The marble rolled across the floor because it was spherical.» Rolling easily is a clue, so spherical must mean round like a ball, not flat or square.
explain: You already know round, but spherical means round in every direction, like a ball. A coin is round but flat, so it is not spherical. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «The orange was ball-shaped» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: In maths, spherical has an exact meaning: every point on the surface is the same distance from the centre. «A spherical object looks the same from every side.» Scientists use it too, so it is a more formal word than round.
fact: Spherical means shaped like a ball, round in every direction.
fact: In maths, every point on the surface of a spherical object is the same distance from the centre.
fact: Oranges, marbles and planets are roughly spherical.
fact: In science, raindrops, bubbles and the Earth are described as nearly spherical.
fact: «Spherical» is a more formal and exact word than «round».
exercise: «The marble was perfectly spherical.» What does spherical mean? | Long and thin like a stick | Square with four equal sides | *Shaped like a ball, round in every direction | Flat and thin like a coin
exercise: In maths, what is true of every point on the surface of a spherical object? | It is always the same colour | *It is the same distance from the centre | It is at the top only | It is closer to the edge than the centre
exercise: Which of these is described in science as nearly spherical? | A straight pencil | A flat sheet of paper | A door | *A raindrop
test: «The bubble floated up, spherical and shining.» Which word is closest in meaning to spherical? | *Ball-shaped | Square | Flat | Sharp
test: Why would a scientist say the Earth is «nearly spherical» rather than «perfectly round»? | Because it is square | Because it is flat | *Because it is not quite a perfect ball | Because it has no surface
exam: Which object is most spherical? | A pencil | *A marble | A sheet of paper | A cube
